body:
Context
- This doc proposes a shared configuration schema for hosted overload protection across edge/gateway, routing/control plane, and runtime.
- Goals:
  - Enable consistent breaker + shedding behavior per (region, model, tier) with safe defaults.
  - Support limited, bounded overrides (per route / per customer tier / per model class) without allowing unsafe configurations.
  - Keep telemetry label cardinality bounded.
  - Work with feature-flag rollout mechanics (enable by region/model) and with policy engine guardrails.

Non-goals
- This schema is not a replacement for quotas / rate limiting.
- Not a general-purpose policy DSL. It is intentionally opinionated and “safe-by-default”.

Design principles
1) A single “effective policy” is computed at request time from:
   - global defaults
   - region overrides
   - model-class overrides
   - model-id overrides
   - tier overrides (hosted tiers)
   - route overrides (OpenAI-compat vs native endpoints; streaming vs non-streaming)
2) Overrides are shallow and bounded. If an override attempts to exceed safety limits, it is rejected at config load time.
3) Breaker logic uses explicit hysteresis/cooldown knobs (ADR-0148). No silent implicit behavior.
4) “Shed action” is always expressed as a reason code + HTTP mapping (ADR-0147) + retry guidance.
5) All shed decisions must be explainable: the layer that sheds must emit (reason_code, layer, retry_after_ms, breaker_key, correlation_id).

Glossary
- breaker_key: the tuple that identifies the breaker state bucket. Proposed: (region, model, tier) with optional “pool” dimension for dedicated pools.
- tier: customer tier classification at gateway (e.g., free, standard, enterprise, internal). Dedicated is treated separately.
- route_class: classification of endpoint type, e.g., chat.completions, responses, embeddings; plus streaming boolean.
- model_class: small set of categories used for tuning defaults, e.g., “small”, “medium”, “large”, “embedding”, “rerank”.
- signal: one input to breaker evaluation, e.g., queue_depth, gpu_utilization, kv_cache_pressure.

Schema draft (conceptual)
- This is a draft representation of the config object that will live in the control plane config store (and be cached at gateway and routing).
- Canonical serialization is JSON. Examples below use JSON-with-comments style for readability.

Top-level object
{
  "schema_version": "0.6",
  "environment": "prod|staging|dev",
  "last_updated_by": "<email or service>",
  "last_updated_at": "YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ",

  "feature_flags": {
    "enabled": true,
    "enable_by_region": ["us-east", "eu-west"],
    "enable_by_model": ["rw-llama-3.1-70b", "rw-mistral-7b"],
    "kill_switch": false
  },

  "defaults": { ... },
  "overrides": { ... },
  "safety_constraints": { ... },
  "telemetry": { ... }
}

Defaults block
"defaults": {
  "breaker": {
    "state_model": "closed-open-half_open",
    "evaluation_interval_ms": 1000,

    "open": {
      "min_open_duration_ms": 15000,
      "cooldown_ms": 30000,
      "half_open_max_probe_rps": 5,
      "half_open_success_threshold": 0.95,
      "half_open_window_ms": 10000
    },

    "hysteresis": {
      "open_on_n_of_m": "3/5",
      "close_on_n_of_m": "4/5",
      "min_state_change_interval_ms": 5000
    },

    "signals": {
      "queue_depth": {
        "enabled": true,
        "open_threshold": 900,
        "close_threshold": 600,
        "window_ms": 5000
      },
      "gpu_saturation": {
        "enabled": true,
        "open_threshold": 0.95,
        "close_threshold": 0.85,
        "window_ms": 10000
      },
      "kv_cache_pressure": {
        "enabled": true,
        "open_threshold": 0.92,
        "close_threshold": 0.80,
        "window_ms": 5000
      }
    }
  },

  "admission": {
    "max_inflight_requests_per_breaker_key": 1200,
    "max_queue_depth": 1000,
    "streaming": {
      "max_concurrent_streams_per_breaker_key": 400,
      "disconnect_on_overload": false
    }
  },

  "shed": {
    "edge": {
      "enabled": true,
      "preferred": true,
      "http_status": 429,
      "error_code": "OVERLOAD_ADMISSION",
      "retry_after_ms": 2000
    },
    "routing": {
      "enabled": true,
      "http_status": 503,
      "error_code": "OVERLOAD_CAPACITY",
      "retry_after_ms": 3000
    },
    "runtime": {
      "enabled": true,
      "http_status": 503,
      "error_code": "OVERLOAD_RUNTIME_QUEUE",
      "retry_after_ms": 3000,
      "shed_points": ["enqueue", "prefill", "decode"]
    }
  },

  "fallback": {
    "enabled": true,
    "max_hops": 1,
    "allowed_dimensions": ["region", "model_variant", "capacity_tier"],
    "require_safety_check": true
  }
}

Overrides block
- Overrides are keyed by selectors. The system merges the most specific match on top of defaults.

"overrides": {
  "by_region": {
    "us-east": {
      "breaker": {
        "signals": {
          "queue_depth": { "open_threshold": 1100, "close_threshold": 800 }
        }
      }
    }
  },

  "by_tier": {
    "enterprise": {
      "fallback": { "enabled": true, "max_hops": 1 },
      "shed": {
        "edge": { "retry_after_ms": 1000 },
        "routing": { "retry_after_ms": 2000 }
      }
    },
    "free": {
      "fallback": { "enabled": false },
      "shed": { "edge": { "retry_after_ms": 5000 } }
    }
  },

  "by_model_class": {
    "large": {
      "admission": { "max_queue_depth": 700 },
      "breaker": {
        "signals": {
          "gpu_saturation": { "open_threshold": 0.93, "close_threshold": 0.83 }
        }
      }
    },
    "embedding": {
      "admission": { "max_queue_depth": 1500 },
      "shed": { "edge": { "http_status": 429, "retry_after_ms": 1000 } }
    }
  },

  "by_model_id": {
    "rw-llama-3.1-70b": {
      "breaker": {
        "open": { "min_open_duration_ms": 20000 }
      }
    }
  },

  "by_route_class": {
    "chat.completions:stream=true": {
      "admission": { "streaming": { "disconnect_on_overload": false } },
      "shed": { "edge": { "http_status": 429, "error_code": "OVERLOAD_ADMISSION_STREAMING" } }
    },
    "embeddings:stream=false": {
      "shed": { "edge": { "http_status": 429, "retry_after_ms": 1000 } }
    }
  }
}

Safety constraints block
- These constraints are enforced at config validation time AND at policy-evaluation time (defensive).

"safety_constraints": {
  "retry_after_ms": {
    "min": 250,
    "max": 30000,
    "quantization_ms": 250
  },

  "breaker": {
    "evaluation_interval_ms": { "min": 500, "max": 5000 },
    "min_open_duration_ms": { "min": 5000, "max": 120000 },
    "cooldown_ms": { "min": 5000, "max": 300000 },
    "half_open_max_probe_rps": { "min": 1, "max": 50 },
    "min_state_change_interval_ms": { "min": 1000, "max": 60000 }
  },

  "admission": {
    "max_queue_depth": { "min": 0, "max": 5000 },
    "max_inflight_requests_per_breaker_key": { "min": 10, "max": 5000 },
    "max_concurrent_streams_per_breaker_key": { "min": 10, "max": 2000 }
  },

  "fallback": {
    "max_hops": { "min": 0, "max": 2 },
    "disallow_cycles": true,
    "require_monotonic_degradation": true,
    "disallow_cross_region_for_tiers": {
      "free": true,
      "standard": false,
      "enterprise": false
    }
  },

  "compat": {
    "openai_compat_error_shape_required": true,
    "allowed_http_statuses": "[429, 503]",
    "disallow_5xx_without_error_code": true
  }
}

Telemetry block
- Naming/label guidance (see observability review notes). Keep label cardinality bounded.

"telemetry": {
  "emit_decision_log": true,
  "emit_trace_annotations": true,
  "metrics": {
    "labels_allowlist": ["region", "model_id", "model_class", "tier", "route_class", "breaker_state", "reason_code"],
    "model_id_label_mode": "allowlist", 
    "model_id_allowlist": ["rw-llama-3.1-70b", "rw-mistral-7b"],
    "sample_rate": {
      "decision_events": 0.05,
      "breaker_transitions": 1.0
    }
  }
}

Reason codes (draft)
- Reason codes are shared across layers; each layer may originate a subset.
- Codes must map to a stable HTTP status + Redwood error object shape (ADR-0147).

Proposed codes:
- OVERLOAD_ADMISSION (gateway admission control)
- OVERLOAD_ADMISSION_STREAMING (streaming-specific admission)
- OVERLOAD_BREAKER_OPEN (routing breaker open)
- OVERLOAD_CAPACITY (routing capacity shortage)
- OVERLOAD_RUNTIME_QUEUE (runtime queue bounded)
- OVERLOAD_RUNTIME_PREFILL (shed at prefill boundary)
- OVERLOAD_RUNTIME_DECODE (shed at decode boundary)
- OVERLOAD_KV_PRESSURE (KV cache / memory pressure guardrail)

Layer ownership / where config is consumed
- Gateway (Amara / API):
  - Reads effective policy for admission + error mapping.
  - Must not implement breaker state machine; it consumes breaker “hints” and config for local admission.
- Routing/control plane (Mina/Ravi):
  - Owns breaker state machine, persistence, hysteresis behavior.
  - Exposes evaluation API and “shed hints” to gateway.
- Runtime (Noah/Lena):
  - Uses admission/queue bounds + shed_points and must emit reason codes.
- Policy engine (Jordan):
  - Validates that customer-configurable fallbacks cannot cause unsafe loops; also validates max_hops, allowed_dimensions.

Examples

Example A: Conservative defaults for us-east + large models
{
  "schema_version": "0.6",
  "environment": "prod",
  "feature_flags": { "enabled": true, "enable_by_region": ["us-east"], "enable_by_model": ["rw-llama-3.1-70b"], "kill_switch": false },
  "defaults": {
    "breaker": {
      "evaluation_interval_ms": 1000,
      "open": { "min_open_duration_ms": 15000, "cooldown_ms": 30000, "half_open_max_probe_rps": 5, "half_open_success_threshold": 0.95, "half_open_window_ms": 10000 },
      "hysteresis": { "open_on_n_of_m": "3/5", "close_on_n_of_m": "4/5", "min_state_change_interval_ms": 5000 },
      "signals": {
        "queue_depth": { "enabled": true, "open_threshold": 900, "close_threshold": 600, "window_ms": 5000 },
        "gpu_saturation": { "enabled": true, "open_threshold": 0.95, "close_threshold": 0.85, "window_ms": 10000 }
      }
    },
    "admission": { "max_inflight_requests_per_breaker_key": 1200, "max_queue_depth": 1000, "streaming": { "max_concurrent_streams_per_breaker_key": 400, "disconnect_on_overload": false } },
    "shed": {
      "edge": { "enabled": true, "preferred": true, "http_status": 429, "error_code": "OVERLOAD_ADMISSION", "retry_after_ms": 2000 },
      "routing": { "enabled": true, "http_status": 503, "error_code": "OVERLOAD_CAPACITY", "retry_after_ms": 3000 },
      "runtime": { "enabled": true, "http_status": 503, "error_code": "OVERLOAD_RUNTIME_QUEUE", "retry_after_ms": 3000, "shed_points": ["enqueue", "prefill", "decode"] }
    },
    "fallback": { "enabled": true, "max_hops": 1, "allowed_dimensions": ["region"], "require_safety_check": true }
  },
  "overrides": {
    "by_region": { "us-east": { "breaker": { "signals": { "queue_depth": { "open_threshold": 1100, "close_threshold": 800 } } } } },
    "by_model_class": { "large": { "admission": { "max_queue_depth": 700 } } }
  },
  "safety_constraints": { "retry_after_ms": { "min": 250, "max": 30000, "quantization_ms": 250 }, "fallback": { "max_hops": { "min": 0, "max": 2 }, "disallow_cycles": true, "require_monotonic_degradation": true } },
  "telemetry": { "emit_decision_log": true, "emit_trace_annotations": true, "metrics": { "labels_allowlist": ["region", "model_id", "model_class", "tier", "route_class", "breaker_state", "reason_code"], "model_id_label_mode": "allowlist", "model_id_allowlist": ["rw-llama-3.1-70b"], "sample_rate": { "decision_events": 0.05, "breaker_transitions": 1.0 } } }
}

Example B: Free tier stricter admission and no fallback
- Motivation: avoid free-tier traffic triggering extra work via fallback, and bias toward early 429 with longer Retry-After.

Override snippet:
"overrides": {
  "by_tier": {
    "free": {
      "fallback": { "enabled": false, "max_hops": 0 },
      "admission": { "max_inflight_requests_per_breaker_key": 600, "max_queue_depth": 500 },
      "shed": { "edge": { "http_status": 429, "retry_after_ms": 8000, "error_code": "OVERLOAD_ADMISSION" } }
    }
  }
}

Example C: Streaming route tweaks
- Motivation: streaming workloads can hold connections open; we cap concurrent streams and prefer edge shed.

Override snippet:
"overrides": {
  "by_route_class": {
    "chat.completions:stream=true": {
      "admission": { "streaming": { "max_concurrent_streams_per_breaker_key": 300 } },
      "shed": { "edge": { "http_status": 429, "retry_after_ms": 3000, "error_code": "OVERLOAD_ADMISSION_STREAMING" } }
    }
  }
}

Validation rules (draft)
1) Any override value outside safety_constraints => reject config load.
2) Allowed HTTP statuses for overload shedding: 429 or 503. (No 500/502 for overload.)
3) If shed.edge.preferred=true then gateway must be enabled for admission control; otherwise reject.
4) If fallback.enabled=true then require max_hops <= safety_constraints.fallback.max_hops.max.
5) Disallow_cycles=true means any configured fallback graph must be acyclic for the allowed_dimensions.
6) require_monotonic_degradation=true means fallback must not increase cost/latency class (e.g., cannot fallback from small->large under overload).
7) For OpenAI-compat routes, the error body must conform to our OpenAI-compatible mapping, including stable error.type and error.code mapping.

Open questions / TODO
- Do we need a separate breaker_key dimension for “route_class” (risk: cardinality explosion)? Current proposal: breaker_key excludes route_class; admission budgets can vary by route_class.
- Dedicated alignment: should Dedicated use the same schema with a different default block (and different safety constraints)? (Tracked in ENG-4837.)
- Where should model_id allowlist live for telemetry? In this doc it’s under telemetry.metrics; observability team may prefer a separate central allowlist service.
- Retry-After selection: static per policy vs dynamic (based on cooldown remaining). Current schema supports static; dynamic behavior should be an implementation detail, but must respect safety_constraints.retry_after_ms.
- Should we support “percent shed” modes (probabilistic) vs deterministic once threshold is hit? Current schema is deterministic; add later if needed.

Change log
- v0.6 (2025-12-15): added telemetry constraints + model_id allowlist, clarified override precedence, expanded reason codes for runtime shed points.
- v0.5 (2025-11-28): added fallback safety constraints (disallow_cycles, monotonic_degradation) and route_class overrides.

Notes to self (Benji)
- Before pushing to Confluence as ADR or standard: get explicit sign-off from Jordan (policy safety), Christine (breaker hysteresis), Brian (error semantics), Allison (metrics/cardinality).
- This needs a companion doc: “override precedence + effective policy computation” with a concrete example and unit tests.
